@startuml

salt
{
  <b>ORE STUDIO - REPORTING: RUN ERRORS</b>
  --
  <b>RUN: Group Consolidated Exposure - 4b7e1a02</b>
  --
  {#
    Finished | Completed | Errors collected | Rows
    completed while carrying errors | 08:15:02 | 08:15:03 | 20
  }
  --
  <b>BY SCOPE AND SEVERITY</b>
  --
  {#
    Scope | error | warning | Total
    Trade | 16 | 0 | 16
    Analytics | 2 | 1 | 3
    Curve | 1 | 0 | 1
    Configuration | 0 | 0 | 0
    Report | 0 | 0 | 0
    Total | 19 | 1 | 20
  }
  --
  <b>FILTER BY SUBJECT</b>
  --
  {
    Subject [ trade ] | Subject id [ 6f2c19a1-... ] | [ Find errors ] | [ Clear ]
  }
  Two rows name this trade. They are kept apart by detail.
  --
  <b>ERROR ROWS</b>
  --
  {#
    # | Severity | Scope | Subject | Subject id | Detail
    1 | error | Curve | curve | IndexCurve(GBP-SONIA,Yield/GBP/GBP1D) | -
    2 | error | Trade | trade | 6f2c19a1-... | PRICING
    3 | error | Trade | trade | 6f2c19a1-... | SA_CCR
    4 | error | Analytics | analytic | PRICING | -
    5 | warning | Analytics | analytic | OREApp::run() | -
  }
  --
  <b>ROW 1 - CURVE ERROR</b>
  --
  {
    Message: yield curve building failed for curve(s) Yield/GBP/GBP1D on date 2026-10-15 while processing Yield/GBP/GBP1D
  }
  --
  <b>ROWS 2 AND 3 - THE SAME TRADE, TWO ANALYTICS</b>
  --
  {#
    # | Scope | Subject | Subject id | Message
    2 | Trade | trade | 6f2c19a1-... | Cannot build all required curves! Building failed for: ([IndexCurve(GBP-SONIA,Yield/GBP/GBP1D)])
    3 | Trade | trade | 6f2c19a1-... | Cannot build all required curves! Building failed for: ([IndexCurve(GBP-SONIA,Yield/GBP/GBP1D)])
  }
  {
    Row 2 detail: {"exceptionType": "Error building trade for context 'analytic/PRICING'"}
  }
  {
    Row 3 detail: {"exceptionType": "Error building trade for context 'analytic/SA_CCR'"}
  }
  The rows are identical in scope, subject, subject id and message. Only detail
  tells them apart. The screen never de-duplicates by message, scope and subject.
  --
  <b>ROW 4 - ANALYTICS ERROR</b>
  --
  {
    Subject: analytic PRICING. Message: Portfolio does not contain any built trades, context is 'analytic/PRICING'
  }
  --
  <b>ROW 5 - ANALYTICS WARNING</b>
  --
  {
    Subject: analytic OREApp::run(). Message: Error in ORE analytics: Failed to run analytics PRICING,SA_CCR
  }
  --
  <b>A CONFIGURATION WARNING, A REAL ROW</b>
  --
  {
    Subject: configuration Counterparty. Message: Input configuration was not provided. The default values will be used for all netting sets in the portfolio
  }
  It names an input and no trade. A run that completed clean can still record
  Configuration warnings: the clean run of this report recorded eight Analytics
  errors and three Configuration warnings.
  --
  <b>A REPORT SCOPE ROW - NO SUBJECT</b>
  --
  {#
    Scope | Severity | Subject | Subject id | Message
    Report | error | none | none | the reason the run failed, stated by the model
  }
  The row names the run itself, for a failure no engine saw. It has no subject
  because a subject without an id is not a row the model admits.
}

@enduml
